Based on the provided content, "Bias Quantification Benchmarks" (child segment 1) is more detailed and provides a comprehensive overview of various metrics used to quantify bias in language models. It discusses embedding-based metrics like WEAT and SEAT, as well as probability-based methods such as StereoSet. This section contributes significantly through the presentation of experimental findings and analysis on how biases can be measured within LLMs.

"Bias Mitigation" (child segment 2) is also important but slightly less so than "Bias Quantification Benchmarks." It outlines various methods for reducing bias in model outputs, including pre-processing techniques like Counter-factual Data Augmentation and projection-based methods such as Iterative Nullspace Projection. While this section contributes through the presentation of mitigation strategies, it is less detailed than "Bias Quantification Benchmarks" regarding specific metrics and experimental findings.

Therefore, I have assigned 57% to "Bias Quantification Benchmarks" and 43% to "Bias Mitigation," reflecting their relative contributions to the parent segment's main scientific contribution.
